															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/darkstuff" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1581620); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1581620&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608498418" alt="DarkStuff" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1581620)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/darkstuff" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1581620); return false;" >DarkStuff</a></span> <span class="odate time_1574274218 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">20 Nov 2019 18:23</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4428018">
									

<p>This is going to be a novote from me, very possibly because I watched a movie that was a non-fiction account of a guy that ran a food truck, and then upgraded to a restaurant, and in that movie there come critics and a lot of the foodie scene gets revealed, and this doesn't jive with me as a realistic representation. But it's not far off. And I'm only limited to one movie I half-remember, so take it with a grain of salt. I don't think that the owners of the restaurant would sit with the critic &#8212; they also might be a little scared of a <em>critic</em> coming to their restaurant, instead of just excited. I would imagine a good deal of nerves. What if the review is negative?</p>
<p>I also think that a guy who eats anomalous food for a living would probably be a little more used to seemingly gross stuff. I mean, in real life, people eat fried tarantulas. Now, not that <em>every</em> food critic gets around to those types of meals &#8212; not every critic gets the &quot;eggs boiled in piss&quot; delicacy &#8212; but those that go after <em>exotic</em> foods likely do, and I'd imagine that the anomalous and exotic have a great deal of overlap. After all, the point of getting into the magical food scene would be to have fantastical new experiences. &quot;Exotic&quot; is a very aptly fitting word.</p>
<p>That said, I like the idea, and he did get over himself pretty quick. Perhaps he is simply a nooby foodie, taking a foray into anomalous food only pretty recently. I could buy it! In any case, this is a novote leaning towards upvote, meaning I am hopeful to read the next chapter.</p>

							</div>

								
					
